…@lower-…@engine-…"},{"id":"spn-49549","text":" sealed + closes"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-33827","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49550","text":"3. A real emitted episode — "},{"id":"spn-49551","marks":["code"],"text":"examples/eval-one/episodes/episode-<id>/"}]},{"id":"blk-33828","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49552","text":"A committed, five-signal 1.0 episode you can "},{"id":"spn-49553","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-49554","text":" directly. Emitted by:"}]},{"id":"blk-33829","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ trvs eval-one examples/eval-one/residency-forge --output examples/eval-one/episodes \\\n      --platform linux-x86_64 -- python3 $PWD/test/fixtures/residency_agent.py\n  status ✓ ok · reward 1 · bundle …/episode-e125d77b…f415\n$ trvs verify-episode examples/eval-one/episodes/episode-e125d77b…f415\n  closure ✓ · artifacts ✓ · citations/patch/tests/identity/finding_completeness ✓\n  reward ✓ (1.0) · episode-id ✓ · verified ✓ closed"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49555","marks":["bold"],"text":"Note on the id:"},{"id":"spn-49556","text":" "},{"id":"spn-49557","marks":["code"],"text":"residency-forge"},{"id":"spn-49558","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-49559","marks":["code"],"text":"task_id"},{"id":"spn-49560","text":" bakes the acceptance command's absolute "},{"id":"spn-49561","marks":["code"],"text":"argv[0]"},{"id":"spn-49562","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-49563","marks":["code"],"text":"sys.executable"},{"id":"spn-49564","text":") — see the prior memo §6.3 — so the emitted "},{"id":"spn-49565","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-<id>"},{"id":"spn-49566","text":" is environment-specific and will differ on your machine. The "},{"id":"spn-49567","marks":["italic"],"text":"shape"},{"id":"spn-49568","text":" and closure are what to review; a fresh "},{"id":"spn-49569","marks":["code"],"text":"--output"},{"id":"spn-49570","text":" run on your box reproduces the same structure with your interpreter's path."}]}],"id":"blk-33830","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-33832","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49571","text":"4. Reclassification you asked me to record"}]},{"id":"blk-33833","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49572","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-49573","marks":["code"],"text":"residency-forge"},{"id":"spn-49574","text":" bundle is a "},{"id":"spn-49575","marks":["bold"],"text":"five-signal conformance fixture"},{"id":"spn-49576","text":" — it exercises the full citations/patch/tests/identity contract deterministically via the stub agent. It is "},{"id":"spn-49577","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-49578","text":" a genuine Evidence Residency "},{"id":"spn-49579","marks":["italic"],"text":"finding"},{"id":"spn-49580","text":" about real code: the \"spec\" and \"src\" are minimal fixtures chosen to make each signal's pass/fail path reachable and byte-reproducible. Treat every reward/verdict in the examples + batteries as a "},{"id":"spn-49581","marks":["bold"],"text":"contract-conformance"},{"id":"spn-49582","text":" demonstration, not a substantive spec-vs-impl result. The first genuine spec/impl task (real repo, real finding) remains future work, gated behind TestPlanV2 + portable toolchain refs (below)."}]},{"id":"blk-33834","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49583","text":"5. New autonomous decisions — please ratify or steer"}]},{"id":"blk-33835","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49584","text":"None move a content-addressed identity beyond Req 3 ("},{"id":"spn-49585","marks":["code"],"text":"verification_evidence"},{"id":"spn-49586","text":" into the allowlist) and Req 7 (the version-string widening) — both of which your ruling directed."}]},{"id":"blk-33836","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49587","marks":["bold"],"text":"Saved evidence files are re-checked against the receipt digest on verify."},{"id":"spn-49588","text":" The"}]}],"id":"blk-33837","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-33839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49589","text":"ruling's replay check compares the "},{"id":"spn-49590","marks":["italic"],"text":"re-run"},{"id":"spn-49591","text":" verifier's digest to the receipt; I also added a check that the "},{"id":"spn-49592","marks":["bold"],"text":"persisted"},{"id":"spn-49593","text":" "},{"id":"spn-49594","marks":["code"],"text":"verifiers/<sig>.json"},{"id":"spn-49595","text":" bytes hash to the receipt digest, so tampering the kept file is caught even if the replay happens to reproduce the same state. (This is what "},{"id":"spn-49596","marks":["code"],"text":"tampered_verifier_evidence_file_rejected"},{"id":"spn-49597","text":" pins.) Say the word if you'd rather the saved file be treated as purely decorative."}]},{"id":"blk-33840","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49598","marks":["bold"],"text":"Runtime tamper (`policy_violations`) is not recomputed on replay."},{"id":"spn-49599","text":" A write-escape"}]}],"id":"blk-33841","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-33843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49600","text":"is a "},{"id":"spn-49601","marks":["italic"],"text":"live-run observation"},{"id":"spn-49602","text":" not recoverable from a digest; replay scores the un-tampered path, and a saved receipt that lies about a tampered reward is caught by the episode-id self-consistency check ("},{"id":"spn-49603","marks":["code"],"text":"tampered_receipt_reward_rejected"},{"id":"spn-49604","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-33844","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33846","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49605","marks":["bold"],"text":"`--json` prints the receipt to stdout; the bundle path goes to stderr."},{"id":"spn-49606","text":" Keeps the"}]}],"id":"blk-33845","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-33847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49607","text":"stdout contract (a pure episode receipt) byte-identical whether or not "},{"id":"spn-49608","marks":["code"],"text":"--output"},{"id":"spn-49609","text":" is set."}]},{"id":"blk-33848","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33850","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49610","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-49611","marks":["code"],"text":"verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-49612","text":" wires "},{"id":"spn-49613","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"},{"id":"spn-49614","text":" unconditionally and "},{"id":"spn-49615","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-49616","text":" when the engine is"}]}],"id":"blk-33849","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-33851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49617","text":"locatable.** An engine-less box that verifies a bundle which scored "},{"id":"spn-49618","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-49619","text":" gets an honest signal "},{"id":"spn-49620","marks":["italic"],"text":"mismatch"},{"id":"spn-49621","text":" (never a false pass), plus a stderr warn."}]},{"id":"blk-33852","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33854","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49622","marks":["bold"],"text":"The manifest carries a non-canonical `created_at`."},{"id":"spn-49623","text":" Wall-clock provenance only;"}]}],"id":"blk-33853","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-33855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49624","text":"it is outside every id and never read on verify."}]},{"id":"blk-33856","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-49625","text":"6. Future (NOT started — awaiting your steer)"}]},{"id":"blk-33857","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-49626","text":"In the order you set: "},{"id":"spn-49627","marks":["bold"],"text":"TestPlanV2 + portable toolchain refs"},{"id":"spn-49628","text":" → the "},{"id":"spn-49629","marks":["bold"],"text":"first genuine spec/impl task"},{"id":"spn-49630","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-49631","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs compare"},{"id":"spn-49632","text":